.TH HIRZD 1 2026-11-16 hirz "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hirzd \- the hirz virtual security key (user daemon)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hirzd
.RB [ \-\-self\-test ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hirzd
makes the user's hirz passkey vault available to browsers and other FIDO2 clients as a USB
security key.
It connects to
.BR hirz\-uhid\-broker (8),
which creates a FIDO HID device for the user, speaks CTAPHID and CTAP2 over it and answers
with the passkeys in the vault.
Every makeCredential and every getAssertion with user presence needs an approval in a hirz
window (zenity): the system password through polkit, a fingerprint through fprintd, a hirz
PIN, or a click for sites listed for click\-to\-allow.
.PP
The vault is opened on the first request and reloaded for every ceremony, so passkeys
created by the Firefox extension path or synced from another device are seen at once.
Without a vault, requests are refused with CTAP2_ERR_NOT_ALLOWED, and hirzd logs a message
and shows a desktop notification at most once every 10 minutes.
.PP
When the broker closes the connection or cannot be reached, hirzd retries after 1 second,
doubling up to 60 seconds; a connection that lasted 30 seconds resets the delay.
.PP
Requests whose relying party id starts with
.B pam://
(pam\-u2f, used for login, sudo and screen unlock) are refused with CTAP2_ERR_NOT_ALLOWED
before the vault is opened and without a prompt, and one line is logged.
hirz passkeys are synced software keys and are not a login factor for the computer they run
on.
OpenSSH keys made with
.B ssh\-keygen \-t ecdsa\-sk
or
.B \-t ed25519\-sk
are shown as "SSH key" in the approval window.
.PP
hirzd is normally started as the systemd user unit
.BR hirzd.service ,
which each user enables with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now hirzd" .
It needs a graphical session for its approval windows.
At start it sets RLIMIT_CORE to 0, PR_SET_DUMPABLE to 0 and PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run a loopback self\-test and exit: create a vault in a temporary folder and play the
browser over an in\-process socket (getInfo, makeCredential, getAssertion with and without
an allow list, a silent probe, and a request without a vault), verifying every signature.
Needs neither root, nor
.IR /dev/uhid ,
nor a desktop.
The approver of the self\-test approves everything and never sees the real vault.
.PP
Any other argument prints a usage message and exits with status 2.
.SH EXIT STATUS
hirzd runs until it is stopped.
It exits with status 1 when it cannot harden itself or locate its folders, and with status 2
on wrong arguments.
.B \-\-self\-test
exits with status 0 when the test passes and 1 otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HIRZ_BROKER_SOCKET
Socket of the broker (default
.IR /run/hirz/uhid.sock ).
.TP
.B HIRZ_VAULT
Vault folder.
Default: the folder recorded in
.I vault\-path
of the state directory, else
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/hirz/vault .
.TP
.B HIRZ_STATE
Device state directory (default
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/hirz ).
.TP
.BR HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base folders; relative values are ignored.
.TP
.B HIRZ_MLOCK
Set to 1 to lock all memory with mlockall.
.TP
.B HIRZ_DEBUG_CTAP
Set to 1 to log every CTAP2 request and response in hex.
They hold client data hashes, relying party ids and credential ids, never keys; keep it off
normally.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hirz/config
Approval configuration, one
.I key " = " value
per line, lines starting with # are comments.
Keys:
.B methods
(verifying methods in order of preference, from
.BR polkit ,
.BR fingerprint ,
.BR pin ),
.B click_to_allow
(comma\-separated relying party ids where a click is enough when the site does not require
verification),
.B timeout
(seconds for a whole request, 10 to 600, default 120) and
.B prompts_per_minute
(per site, 1 to 60, default 5).
An invalid file makes every approval fail until it is fixed.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/hirz
Device state, including the hirz PIN verifier.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/hirzd.service
The systemd user unit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hirz (1),
.BR hirz\-uhid\-broker (8),
.BR hirz\-nmh (1),
.BR pkcheck (1),
.BR zenity (1)
.PP
.I docs/uhid.md
and
.I docs/approval.md
in the hirz sources.
